WEBVTT

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.120
It's true this guy touched her thigh.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.660
But 100,000 yen for a single bottle of beer?

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.790
Those are the rules.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:22.290
See?

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.160
"Entrance Fee"
"Subtotal"
"Service Fee"
"Total Amount Due"

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.910
Such fine print...

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.790
All right...

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.000
...I'll pay the 100,000 yen.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.160
Takuya.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.120
In exchange, I'll need 100,000 for his
hospital bills and 50,000 for his glasses.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.450
You are quite the joker.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.120
Okay. Okay. That's enough.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.750
Will you take the hit this time, for my sake?

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.750
Who the hell are you?!

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:53.580
We can't do that, Mr. Kaibara. There are rules.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:58.910
I heard you guys have a pretty
big deal going down soon.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.040
I'll keep it quiet from the police.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.160
I'd appreciate that.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.080
Get back to your stations.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.000
Who're you?

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.540
Wanna get some ramen?

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:55.000
"AFTERLOST"

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.080
"Episode 7: Regret"

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:01.040
"Episode 7: Regret"
Lacuna is a major company!

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:05.000
I had no idea our facility
was connected to them...

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.450
Because of that, the police
can't really do anything.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.830
We need solid evidence to crush them.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:16.540
The problem is that the academy
is in the lock-down district.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.750
It's heartening we have people
who know what it's like inside.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:27.580
Are those your real feelings?
Do you really feel this is right?

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.620
Oh? Are you making a new flower bed?

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.700
It's an underground shelter.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:46.660
We have no idea what will happen...
so I thought I'd take this chance.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.290
The Japanese anemone. Beautiful.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:54.080
They've grown well.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.330
Did something happen?

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:00.540
Though small, there was a
change of gravitational waves.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.250
As I thought...

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.250
Here.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:09.950
Thank you.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:14.700
Wasn't Takuya from the same
detective agency as you, Miss Yumiko?

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.080
Yes, until the Lost.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.160
So he's been like that since then...

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.120
Are you curious? About Takuya's past.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:39.250
I should take this chance to tell you
the reason he's now a lone wolf courier.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:43.580
And the reason he's so hung up on contracts.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:50.160
It's a small agency,
but it makes us close, like family.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:55.040
Yumiko, this is Takuya. Take care of him.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.620
Yes.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.410
Well. Try your best without overdoing it.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:06.290
Mr. Kaibara said that, but you shouldn't
get involved with half-hearted feelings.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:10.910
This is a dangerous job, there are
times we take illegal measures.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.370
Fifty more.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.200
I don't know whether it was
dedication or innate talent,

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.750
but Takuya's skills just
got better and better.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.290
Before I realized it,
he was the ace of our agency.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:40.120
She's got some mileage on her,
but she runs great. Take care of her.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.500
Why a scooter?

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.700
Detectives and scooters go together!

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:45.910
Here.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:53.870
I'll take care of thing here, okay?

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.200
Even if it's you, Mr. Kakizaki...

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.580
Help me out here.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:58.910
Let's go on patrol.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.200
Huh?

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.870
One hour is the best we can do.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.910
Got it. Thanks.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.540
An undercover investigation.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.080
The Ministry of Health, Labor, and Welfare

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:13.120
wants to investigate a possible case
of abuse in a certain orphanage.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.120
Abuse...

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.620
Then, I'm perfect for the job!

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.250
I'm good with people, and kids love me!

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:25.700
No, this time I want Takuya to go.
Will you do it?

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.290
Yes.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.120
You'll be infiltrating the Light of Hope
Academy for Disabled Children.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:32.370
"Light of Hope Academy for Disabled Children"
You'll be infiltrating the Light of Hope
Academy for Disabled Children.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.370
"Light of Hope Academy for Disabled Children"

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.870
It's in such decay...

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:41.660
It's been three years since the Lost.
The whole lock-down district is like this.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:44.540
I hope there's some solid evidence left in here.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.200
Let's go.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.700
Take this! Continuous Fire Attack!

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:08.750
Takahiko?!

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.250
Why is there a kid here?!

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.910
Hey, Takahiko!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.290
You didn't clean the rabbit hutch again!

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:16.500
I'm gonna tell Teacher Mama!

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.950
Whoa! A noisy girl appeared! Poof!

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:21.080
Karin...

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.540
Big Brother Takuya.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.620
Did you buy the bananas?

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.500
Naoya...

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:31.410
Mr. Takuya, welcome home.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:34.080
Ayano... Miss Hinako...

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:37.870
Everyone! The baby chicks have
finally hatched from their eggs!

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.290
Really?! Yay!

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.000
Can we touch them?

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.250
They were just born, so you can't touch them!

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.160
If you are free, Mr. Takuya...

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.410
Teacher Mama is saying that she's lonely
without you, Big Brother Takuya!

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:54.830
M-My! W-We'll go on ahead!

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.000
Are they...?

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:04.290
Yeah. Tama-shi. Both her and those children.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:08.700
They were caught in the Lost on the
day they went to see the circus.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.790
Light of Hope Academy for Disabled Children...

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:20.290
They have a connection with you.
The things that were happening there...

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:23.910
The suspected child abuse...

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:29.870
It was Takuya's mission to find out the truth.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:32.200
There are chicks in there?

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:34.700
Look. They've peeked out.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.830
Whoa! So cute!

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.870
Shh! Don't be so loud.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.080
Yeah.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.330
A world made by Tama-shi, huh?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.700
How do we get out of here?

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:48.250
As far as I know,

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:53.330
the only way out is for the Tama-shi who
made it to be released from their regret.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:58.950
So we have to figure out
who created this world.

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:02.080
It's me.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:05.330
All that chirping. They're just like all of you.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:07.200
That's so mean, Big Brother Takuya!

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.830
We're not that noisy.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:11.330
No. No.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:15.330
I'm saying that you'll all fly from the nest
to anywhere you want soon enough.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:16.870
Us?

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.500
Yeah. Once you're all adults.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:23.120
The things you want to become.
I'm sure you'll be able to become them.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:24.200
Really?

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.500
Yeah. I'm sure of it.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.910
Ayano?

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.370
Then, I want to become a soccer player!

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.750
I want to become a veterinarian!

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:34.830
What about you, Naoya?

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.040
Huh?

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:41.120
I love math, so I want to become a math teacher.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:47.290
But the principal and Teacher Mama
say we can't think like that.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.160
Why?

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:54.540
It is the philosophy of this academy
that one must be of use to the people.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.660
More than what one wants to become, we try
to teach what they should be for others.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:03.410
Isn't that kind of life more noble?

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.660
The principal always told me that, too.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:12.000
I remember now. That Hinako person was
at the academy when I was there, too.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:15.290
So she was from the academy, herself?

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:17.830
All the way until the Lost...

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:22.200
Her entire world was this academy.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:26.700
The academy was not doing well financially.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:33.080
If Lacuna was giving them financial support,
there should be some hidden record books.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:35.500
We'll just have to search
with a fine tooth comb.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.830
Ayano.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:43.450
Here. I made this with the Japanese
anemones from the garden.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.910
They're beautiful.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:48.120
Your dream was to become the
owner of a flower shop, right?

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:53.120
Thank you.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:05.290
Looks like you're properly registered as
"Mr. Takuya" in this world.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.790
We should avoid contact as
much as possible. Let's go.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:12.700
The number you have dialed is currently
in an area that cannot be reached or...

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:15.250
Huh?! Why isn't it connecting?

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:17.540
We're almost out of time!

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.040
I'll take that!

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.040
Then, I'll have one more.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.200
It's snack time. They had
that when I was here, too.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:37.950
I was always sent out to buy ingredients
for dinner during that time.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:42.000
Did everyone eat their snacks?
Then, let's take what we always do.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.870
Okay.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:52.450
Your grades haven't been good lately, Ayano.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:55.040
Why not take another two red ones?

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.580
Yes...

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:02.540
Hey, do you know what the
Japanese anemone symbolizes?

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:04.330
No...

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.620
Patience.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.120
What a strange sight.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:15.290
It was part of our daily lives, though.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:16.750
Mr. Takuya!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.120
Shit!

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:21.000
Why didn't I realize?!

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.580
Mr. Takuya...

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.330
Their future dreams?

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.830
Who made them write something like this?

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:28.580
That is...

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.950
It's the principal.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:33.750
Was it Takuya?

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:38.200
So unnecessary. It seems he
doesn't fit in well with us.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:42.290
I hope you haven't been affected by him.

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:43.830
Of course not!

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:46.790
Do not disappoint me!

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:48.040
Of course.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.830
You were the one who took me in,

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:56.830
an unchosen failure who
is useless to this world.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:13:00.000
As long as you understand.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:18.910
In that academy, there was a gifted class
that only talented children attended.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:21.580
It was an honor to be chosen.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:34.580
Naoya was chosen?

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:38.160
Where do the chosen children go every week?

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.160
They go to meet potential foster parents.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:43.950
I want to go with them next time.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:46.330
I don't think the principal
will give you permission.

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:49.910
Why? Are they doing something suspicious?

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:52.540
Both my brother and I were chosen.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:56.120
That was when my brother's power manifested.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:14:00.410
That's why he left, so he
wouldn't be used by the Agency!

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.410
Answer me, Miss Hinako.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:06.330
I want those children to be happy.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:09.790
The children <i>are </i>happy.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:11.200
Huh?

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:15.120
Those children... were tossed aside by everyone.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.450
Even their parents didn't want them.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:23.160
Now those children are being of use to someone.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:26.290
Is there greater happiness than that?

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.950
Are those your real feelings?

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:31.870
Do you really feel this is right?

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.870
Yes.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:44.950
If I had faced her more properly...

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.660
Mr. Takuya...

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:52.120
This is all in the past. Let's think
of what we can do now, Takuya.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:58.620
Human experimentation?!
The same thing that was being done to me...

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:02.830
Takuya had already started
figuring out the truth.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:07.080
He was so close, but...

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.250
What do you mean we're stopping?!

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:14.620
Just like I said. There's no longer any
need to go undercover at the academy.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:15.870
The reason?

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.000
It's already been decided.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:20.700
I can't accept this! I am so close to the truth!

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:26.700
Remember this, Takuya. We aren't the police.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.370
And, we're definitely not heroes of justice.

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:30.830
Mr. Kaibara!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.080
Why so suddenly?

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:41.910
I don't really know why
Mr. Kaibara had a change of heart.

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:45.000
However, the orders from above are absolute.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:49.080
Especially in an agency that
deals with dangerous missions.

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:52.750
I can't imagine Takuya listening obediently.

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.910
That may be true now.

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:01.500
So detectives do the same
things as thieves, sometimes.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:04.410
Shut up. I can't hear.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:10.200
Why is Mr. Kaibara here?

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:10.950
Mr. Takuya?

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:13.000
I told you, I can't hear!

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:18.950
He's hot-blooded. It must have been
something really worth looking into.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:23.750
You must be kidding.
There's nothing to find here.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.580
So? What's going to happen to the children?

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:29.450
That is not for me to decide.

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:31.200
Why?

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.790
Aren't they pretty?

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:35.200
This is my favorite.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:42.950
Mr. Takuya?

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:48.500
Even though our agency pulled out,
I should have kept investigating!

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:54.790
Someone gave us circus tickets.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.290
Would you like to come with us?

00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:58.450
It's that day.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:01.410
That day? You mean, the Lost?

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.700
Sorry, I can't go with you.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:04.540
Huh?

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:09.700
I'm submitting my resignation.
I'm quitting as of today.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:12.450
So, our superiors said something.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:18.250
That's too bad. I was hoping you would
at least be able to go with us here.

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:23.950
Now that I think of it,
we never went anywhere together.

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:25.370
I'm sorry.

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:28.580
Hey!

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:30.910
Let's go already!

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:33.540
So I guess this is where we part ways.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:35.870
Our time together was so short...

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.370
Wait!

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:50.000
You can't go!

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:52.500
So passionate!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.870
Get married! Get married!

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:59.870
Sorry. I'm... I'm really sorry.

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:03.500
Why are you apologizing?

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:08.040
Such a strange person.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.290
I've finally decided.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:17.950
Once we come back from the circus,
I'm going to tell the children the truth.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:24.910
I want to tell them that they have
unlimited possibilities in their futures.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:29.080
It's thanks to you, Mr. Takuya.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:32.870
Lastly...

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:39.410
...please clean out the birdhouse for us.

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.370
Miss Hinako.

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:04.700
We're back.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.120
Mr. Takuya?

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:19.290
Takuya quit our agency right after that.

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:31.160
Even so, Takuya still rides that
scooter because, somewhere in his heart,

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:34.750
he still wants to believe in Mr. Kaibara.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:44.950
Since we're back... Does that mean we
released Miss Hinako from her regret?

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:53.450
The documents in the safe were all trash.
A total waste of time!

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.750
Lastly...

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:03.040
...please clean out the birdhouse for us.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.870
What are you doing?

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:15.750
"Financial Registry"

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.410
That's...!

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.620
It's the cash book that
Miss Hinako kept record of.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:22.410
"Item || Income || Expense"

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:24.620
"Item || Income || Expense"
There are deposits from Lacuna!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:29.120
This is solid evidence that the academy
and Lacuna were connected.

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:34.120
We can attack the Agency with this!
Now we just need a living witness...

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:37.080
I will take on that role.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:38.120
Huh?

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:42.870
The public will pay attention
because they know of me.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:48.620
Yoshiaki. Are you sure?
You might lose everything.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:52.750
I finally realized what I need to do.

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:56.120
I think my brother would wish
for me to do this, too.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:59.950
Got it. I'm depending on you.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:05.620
Takuya?

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.330
Welcome home.

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:21.700
I'm home.

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:28.910
Yuki. Sorry, there's something I want
to do before we head to Lost.

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:30.540
It can't be helped.

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:31.620
Huh?

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:35.040
Make sure to explain everything to me later.

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:36.500
Sorry...

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:39.950
You should say "thank you," not "sorry."

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.910
Yeah.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:49.660
What's wrong?

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:52.000
I've seen this person before.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.410
I've seen him at the research
facility multiple times.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:56.910
What did you say?

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:59.620
I thought he was disposed of by the Agency...

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:01.750
They sheltered him instead?

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:03.200
Takuya...

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:37.950
"AFTERLOST"

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:46.200
Next Episode: "Choice."
